      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "The start frame anchors frame one and argues for nothing after it. Everything that\nmust hold across the clip goes in the motion prompt: camera direction, what moves,\nwhat stays still, and that it continues for the whole shot.\n\nMotion is a FIXED BUDGET, not a rate. Doubling the length does not double the\nmovement, it spreads the same movement thinner. A long shot reads slower and\neventually nearly static. For a moving sequence, cut several short shots."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
